  "text": "```verilog\nmodule apbslave #(\n\tparameter\tC_APB_ADDR_WIDTH = 12,\n\tparameter\tC_APB_DATA_WIDTH = 32,\n\tlocalparam\tAW = C_APB_ADDR_WIDTH,\n\tlocalparam\tDW = C_APB_DATA_WIDTH,\n\tlocalparam\tAPBLSB = $clog2(C_APB_DATA_WIDTH)-3\n) (\n\tinput\twire\t\t\tPCLK, PRESETn,\n\tinput\twire\t\t\tPSEL,\n\tinput\twire\t\t\tPENABLE,\n\toutput\treg\t\t\tPREADY,\n\tinput\twire\t\t[AW-1:0]\tPADDR,\n\tinput\twire\t\t\tPWRITE,\n\tinput\twire\t\t[DW-1:0]\tPWDATA,\n\tinput\twire\t\t[DW/8-1:0]\tPWSTRB,\n\tinput\twire\t\t[2:0]\t\tPPROT,\n\toutput\treg\t\t[DW-1:0]\tPRDATA,\n\toutput\twire\t\t\tPSLVERR\n);\n\n\tlocalparam\tNUM_BYTES = DW/8;\n\tlocalparam\tNUM_WORDS = 1; // Assuming single word access for simplicity in this generic model\n\tlocalparam\tADDR_MASK = ~((1<<AW)-1);\n\n\treg\t[AW-1:0]\tADDR_REG;\n\treg\t[DW-1:0]\tDATA_REG;\n\treg\t\t\tSTATE; // IDLE, SETUP, ACCESS\n\treg\t\t\tTRANS_DONE;\n\treg\t\t\tVALID;\n\treg\t\t\tPROT_MATCH;\n\n\t// State Machine\n\talways @(posedge PCLK or negedge PRESETn) begin\n\t\tif (!PRESETn) begin\n\t\t\tSTATE <= IDLE;\n\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\tPRDATA <= 0;\n\t\t\tPSLVERR <= 1'b0;\n\t\t\tADDR_REG <= 0;\n\t\t\tDATA_REG <= 0;\n\t\t\tTRANS_DONE <= 1'b0;\n\t\t\tVALID <= 1'b0;\n\t\t\tPROT_MATCH <= 1'b1;\n\t\tend\n\t\telse begin\n\t\t\tcase (STATE)\n\t\t\t\tIDLE: begin\n\t\t\t\t\tif (PSEL && PENABLE) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\tSTATE <= SETUP;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tADDR_REG <= PADDR;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPROT_MATCH <= 1'b1; // Assume valid for now\n\t\t\t\t\t\tVALID <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b0;\n\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\t\telse begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t\tSETUP: begin\n\t\t\t\t\tif (PSEL && PENABLE) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\tSTATE <= ACCESS;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b0;\n\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\t\telse begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t\tACCESS: begin\n\t\t\t\t\tif (PSEL && PENABLE) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// Handle Write\n\t\t\t\t\t\tif (PWRITE) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// Byte strobe handling\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfor (integer i = 0; i < NUM_BYTES; i = i + 1) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif (PWSTRB[i]) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDATA_REG[i*8 +: 8] <= PWDATA[i*8 +: 8];\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// Handle Read (Data is loaded from register on read cycle)\n\t\t\t\t\t\telse begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// Data is already in DATA_REG from previous setup or initial state\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// In a real implementation, you might have a separate read data register\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// Here we assume DATA_REG holds the value to be read\n\t\t\t\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\tTRANS_DONE <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tVALID <= 1'b0;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tSTATE <= IDLE;\n\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\t\telse begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tendcase\n\t\tend\n\tend\n\n\t// Output Logic\n\tassign PSLVERR = (STATE == ACCESS && !PWRITE && !VALID) ? 1'b0 : 1'b0; // Simplified error logic\n\t// In a robust design, PSLVERR would be asserted if PSEL goes low during ACCESS without TRANS_DONE\n\t// or if address is invalid. For this basic model, we assume valid addresses.\n\t// Correcting PSLVERR logic based on standard APB: Error if PSEL is low during ACCESS phase and TRANS_DONE is not set\n\t// However, since we transition to IDLE immediately after TRANS_DONE, PSLVERR is typically 0 unless protocol violation.\n\t// Let's assert error if PSEL is low while we are in ACCESS state and TRANS_DONE is not yet set (violation of setup time)\n\t// But the FSM above handles the clock edge. A simpler approach for this specific request:\n\t// Assert error if PSEL is low during the ACCESS phase (which shouldn't happen in correct usage)\n\t// Or simply 0 for this basic implementation as no specific error conditions are modeled beyond protocol.\n\t// Let's stick to 0 for this basic model as per \"ordinary setup and access phases\" requirement without complex error injection.\n\tassign PSLVERR = 1'b0; \n\n\t// Read Data Output\n\tassign PRDATA = DATA_REG;\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>\n<|endoftext|>",
